-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §22: in a special-education school of several
-- stages that is not one of §21's, a teacher works by the grades taught —
-- grades 1–6 the primary special-education week, grades 7–9 and from 10 up
-- the junior-high special-education week (the latter subject to the wages
-- commissioner's letter of 25.12.08).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-common`
IMPORT `base-agreement-18`
§ `22 מורה בבית ספר לחינוך מיוחד הכולל מספר שלבי חינוך`

-- akn:art_22 The opening: who the clause applies to; the rules are (א)–(ג).

-- (ג) is "subject to" a letter the corpus does not hold; what the letter
-- adds or takes away is an input, so the rule says only what (ג) itself
-- gives.
@ref akn:art_22__para_a akn:art_22__para_b akn:art_22__para_c
GIVEN `lowest grade taught` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the week in a multi-stage special-education school` `lowest grade taught` IS
    IF `lowest grade taught` AT MOST 6
    THEN `a special-education teacher's full week` `a primary school`
    ELSE `a special-education teacher's full week` `a junior high school`

#ASSERT `the week in a multi-stage special-education school` 3 EQUALS `a week of` 26 5 5
#ASSERT `the week in a multi-stage special-education school` 8 EQUALS `a week of` 23 4 9
#ASSERT `the week in a multi-stage special-education school` 11 EQUALS `a week of` 23 4 9
